WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.463
- It's over, Anakin. I
have the high ground.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.043
- You underestimate my power.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.100
- The force is very strong over at Disney,

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.170
which last week announced a
galactic federation's worth

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.790
of Star Wars content coming
to our big and small screens

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:16.870
over the next few years.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.180
But don't you worry because
we're gonna bite-size

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.600
this bantha down for you

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.600
by focusing on three different titles

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.100
right now on The Ketchup.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.700
Disney's Investor Day was a
cornucopia of content this year,

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.500
with over 50 new series
and movies announced.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.110
When it was Star Wars' turn at the mic,

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:35.360
Lucasfilm's Kathleen Kennedy
confirmed two feature films

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.890
and 10 new Disney+ shows rolling out

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.260
over the next several years.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.990
First up, Hayden Christensen

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:42.630
is reentering the Star Wars universe

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.260
for the upcoming Obi-Wan
series, starring Ewan McGregor.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.220
Can you tell I'm excited?

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.350
Set 10 years after "Revenge Of The Sith"

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.100
and a decade before "A New Hope,"

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:54.260
the show will focus on Ben
Kenobi's lost years on Tatooine.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.460
And I, for one, can't
wait to see how Obi goes

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.060
from looking like Ewan to
Alec Guinness in 20 years,

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.230
but maybe he forgot to
wear his two sunscreens.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.063
Get it?

00:01:02.063 --> 00:01:04.000
- I felt a great disturbance in the force.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.710
- Kennedy teased that
the show would feature

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.980
a confrontation between the Jedi master

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.130
and his former padawan,

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.890
after the two last faced off on Mustafar -

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:13.840
a fight which cost Obi-Wan his faith,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.850
and Anakin an arm and two legs.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.357
Kennedy actually referred
to the showdown as

00:01:18.357 --> 00:01:20.580
"The rematch of the century."

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.520
No disrespect, but it seems kind of like

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.710
an inaccurate assessment
of these guys' history,

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.990
considering the next time
Vader and Obi-Wan meet again

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.100
in "A New Hope," one of
them gets sliced in half

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.230
by a lightsaber.

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.070
Last time we checked,
it's hard to top murder

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.330
in the epic rematch
category, but who knows?

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.990
The long-awaited series,

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.230
which was allegedly
scrapped back in January

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.700
and put on hold while
the concept was retooled,

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.360
still has a number of question marks,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.060
ranging from release date
to the number of episodes.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.440
But low key, this kind of gives me hope

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.040
that maybe the Lizzie McGuire
series will come back to life.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.170
But anyway, our number one question

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:54.350
is will James Earl
Jones make a vocal cameo

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.100
now that Anakin has his helmet on?

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.080
As far as what we do know,

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.500
the show will start
filming in March of 2021,

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.530
and at the helm is Deborah Chow.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:02.877
Now, Chow recently directed

00:02:02.877 --> 00:02:05.470
"The Mandalorian" Season
178 penultimate episode,

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:06.480
so we know she's good

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.160
at getting great
helmet-based performances.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.200
- [The Armorer] This is the way.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.033
- While the Obi-Wan series

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.350
will be sandwiched between
the events of the prequels

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:16.580
and the original trilogy, the
upcoming "Rogue Squadron" film

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.040
will be giving us our
most futuristic glimpse

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.900
into the Star Wars universe yet.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.040
And no, we're not just talking
about the release date,

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.030
which right now is slated

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.830
for a very distant-sounding
Christmas 2023.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.710
First formed by Luke Skywalker,

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.600
the Rogue Squadron has already
been the subject of games

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.220
and novelizations over the years,

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.560
but director Patty Jenkins
stated that her movie

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.460
will be an entirely original
story set in a future era,

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.720
introducing audiences to a
new generation of pilots.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.260
As the first female director
of a Star Wars movie,

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:48.400
Jenkins is already pushing the
franchise in a new direction,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.150
away from the Skywalker saga.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.810
And in a Twitter video released

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.510
shortly after the Disney announcement,

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:54.820
she said that she was inspired

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.730
by her father's death in the Air Force

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.540
to make the greatest fighter
pilot movie of all time.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:03.109
So expect more "Top Gun" than "Rogue One."

00:03:03.109 --> 00:03:04.610
- That's one hell of a pilot!

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:07.430
- Before Rosario Dawson's
non-animated debut

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:08.740
in this season of "The Mandalorian,"

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.610
fans were rightly demanding to know

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.160
where the dank farrik was a Ahsoka Tano.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.010
And now we know.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.750
The beloved character
from "The Clone Wars"

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.030
and "Rebels" cartoon series

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.650
will be getting her own
live-action spinoff.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.300
But first, some backstory.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.410
Having been trained by
none other than Anakin,

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.510
Ahsoka never became a full Jedi,

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.890
instead defecting to help the resistance.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.610
She later teamed up with a young Jedi

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:32.670
named Ezra Bridger after he
reached through time and space

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:33.960
and saved her from Darth Vader,

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.320
but lost contact after he disappeared

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.150
on a ship set to hyperspace

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.400
while fighting Grand Admiral Thrawn.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.700
Now, in "The Mandalorian"

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.400
Ahsoka is still looking for Thrawn,

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.640
so we can assume that the show

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.010
will continue her quest to find Ezra

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:49.320
and suss out the Thrawn,
which could also tie in

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.157
with another upcoming Star Wars series,

00:03:51.157 --> 00:03:52.580
"Rangers Of The New Republic."

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.610
But we'll have to break down "Rangers"

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.217
and the other new
series, "Lando," "Andor,"

00:03:57.217 --> 00:04:00.100
"The Bad Batch," "The
Acolyte" another day.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.460
Not to mention, the new, untitled

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.860
Taika Waititi Star Wars film.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.060
And Disney clearly
wasn't done with the news

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.677
because they just announced
another spinoff series,

00:04:08.677 --> 00:04:12.260
"The Book Of Boba Fett,"
coming to Disney+ in 2021.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.070
Right now, little is
known about the series,

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.530
but stay tuned for more on that

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:16.560
'cause we'll be breaking down

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.730
what the finale of "Mandalorian" Season 2

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.930
means for the future
of Star Wars next time.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:24.830
- There are too many of them,
what are we going to do?

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:25.980
- All right friends, it's time for us

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:27.470
to force throw it over to you, now.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:29.150
Is this finally enough Star Wars content

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.220
to make your little heart sing?

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:31.750
Are you low-key upset that Jar Jar Binks

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.740
doesn't have his own spinoff yet?

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.880
I am. But let us know all
your thoughts and feelings

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.713
in the comments section.

00:04:36.713 --> 00:04:39.240
And of course, if you want
more Disney investor news,

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.130
head on over to RottenTomatoes.com.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.250
As always, we cannot thank
you enough for watching

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:44.930
another episode of "The Ketchup."

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.460
My name's Naz Perez, and
may the force be with you.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.127
(upbeat music)

